  <h2>Overview</h2>

  <p><strong>Thursday, September 10</strong> — Optional early arrival. Settle in, meet your fellow participants, evening social.</p>
  <p><strong>Friday, September 11</strong> — Main arrival day. Orientation, evening dance.</p>
  <p><strong>Saturday, September 12</strong> — Full day: morning workshops, afternoon unconference sessions, evening dance.</p>
  <p><strong>Sunday, September 13</strong> — Morning sessions, afternoon wind-down, closing circle, evening gathering. Event ends Sunday night.</p>
  <p><strong>Monday, September 14</strong> — Optional late departure for those staying the extra night.</p>

  <h2>Unconference Sessions</h2>

  <p>A big part of Kin-Fusion is the unconference — participant-led sessions proposed and scheduled by attendees. You can <a href="/unconference/">propose a workshop or session</a> when you register. The schedule is built collaboratively on-site.</p>

  <p><em>Detailed timing will be shared with confirmed participants closer to the event.</em></p>
